# scowld: upstream tests (tests/parity/upstream_scowld_*/) that tests/flows/test_upstream.py
# does not run against the ported flow, one per line: <test id>  <why>. Every other test of the
# app's own suite runs unchanged against store_release/flows/scowld/.
test_ios_release.CreativeGateTests.test_every_ios_switch_is_printed_and_documented  reads the app's store/gates.env.example, which store-release's own gates.env.example and docs/switches.md replace (tests/workflows/test_docs.py)
test_ios_release.LocalInputTests.test_committed_store_metadata_is_valid  reads the app's committed store files or source (listing, screenshots, catalog against the app); the app's Store checks run these through `ios pr-checks` / `catalog check`
test_ios_release.PrintGatesTests.test_invalid_values_are_shown_as_invalid  tests the app's scripts/store/print_gates.py; store-release prints the switches with `run.py print-switches` (tests/unit/test_core.py)
test_ios_release.PrintGatesTests.test_live_switches_warn  tests the app's scripts/store/print_gates.py; store-release prints the switches with `run.py print-switches` (tests/unit/test_core.py)
test_ios_release.PrintGatesTests.test_reports_exactly_what_the_gates_parse  tests the app's scripts/store/print_gates.py; store-release prints the switches with `run.py print-switches` (tests/unit/test_core.py)
test_ios_release.PrintGatesTests.test_unset_off_and_ignored_switches  tests the app's scripts/store/print_gates.py; store-release prints the switches with `run.py print-switches` (tests/unit/test_core.py)
test_ios_release.RedactLogsTests.test_empty_ids_never_match_everything  tests the app's log redactor; store-release redacts with `run.py ios redact-logs`, a superset of every app's rules (tests/unit/test_flows.py RedactUnionTests)
test_ios_release.RedactLogsTests.test_file_that_can_be_neither_rewritten_nor_dropped_fails  tests the app's log redactor; store-release redacts with `run.py ios redact-logs`, a superset of every app's rules (tests/unit/test_flows.py RedactUnionTests)
test_ios_release.RedactLogsTests.test_file_that_cannot_be_rewritten_is_dropped  tests the app's log redactor; store-release redacts with `run.py ios redact-logs`, a superset of every app's rules (tests/unit/test_flows.py RedactUnionTests)
test_ios_release.RedactLogsTests.test_missing_folder_is_not_an_error  tests the app's log redactor; store-release redacts with `run.py ios redact-logs`, a superset of every app's rules (tests/unit/test_flows.py RedactUnionTests)
test_ios_release.RedactLogsTests.test_symlinks_are_removed_not_followed  tests the app's log redactor; store-release redacts with `run.py ios redact-logs`, a superset of every app's rules (tests/unit/test_flows.py RedactUnionTests)
test_ios_release.RedactLogsTests.test_text_binary_and_utf16_files_are_all_redacted  tests the app's log redactor; store-release redacts with `run.py ios redact-logs`, a superset of every app's rules (tests/unit/test_flows.py RedactUnionTests)
test_ios_release.ReleaseNotesTests.test_committed_release_notes_have_one_section_per_heading  tests the app's scripts/release_notes.py; store-release reads the notes with `run.py release-notes` (same section rules; tests/unit/test_flows.py ReleaseNotesRulesTests)
test_ios_release.ReleaseNotesTests.test_duplicate_sections_for_the_tag_fail  tests the app's scripts/release_notes.py; store-release reads the notes with `run.py release-notes` (same section rules; tests/unit/test_flows.py ReleaseNotesRulesTests)
test_ios_release.ReleaseNotesTests.test_matching_section_missing_section_and_empty_section  tests the app's scripts/release_notes.py; store-release reads the notes with `run.py release-notes` (same section rules; tests/unit/test_flows.py ReleaseNotesRulesTests)
test_ios_release.ReleaseNotesTests.test_missing_notes_file_means_generated_notes  tests the app's scripts/release_notes.py; store-release reads the notes with `run.py release-notes` (same section rules; tests/unit/test_flows.py ReleaseNotesRulesTests)
